Port: an X11 display backend, and display backends that decline gracefully.

WPE draws through Wayland, DRM or nothing. This adds wpe/x11, a small X11
backend (one window per toplevel, frames copied with XPutImage, core
protocol input), registered below Wayland and above headless, so
wpe_display_get_default() tries Wayland, then X11, then renders offscreen.

With ZEBKIT_OPTIONAL_SYSTEM_LIBRARIES (profiles/include/size-prelude.h) the
display libraries are loaded on demand (deps/syslibs), and the Wayland
backend first checks that a new enough libwayland-client exists instead of
assuming it. Without ENABLE_WPE_PLATFORM_X11 and that define, behaviour is
unchanged.

